      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T07:07:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why exclude only control characters ? There\u0027s a lot of characters that are not printable properly in logs, and covering this completely here would be hard. If we have strings with non-breakable spaces or zero-length spaces.\n\nIt would be easier to fallback to hex for anything non-obvious; for example if any character is `!Character.isLetterOrDigit \u0026\u0026 char !\u003d \u0027 \u0027` (you could include Character.isIdeographic but in practice we\u0027d probably be fine debugging with hex when they\u0027re used ?)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 593,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 593,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "64b10d83740be32afbb6c5de0711fc2094c9a620",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
